# ============================================================================
# IntelliFi_anomaly_detection — .gitignore
# Rule of thumb: commit CODE, SPECS, DOCS and the small RESULT artifacts
# (docs/*.json, docs/*.md, docs/*.csv). NEVER commit the datasets, derived
# parquet, snapshots, logs, secrets or caches — the data/ store alone is ~97 GB
# (v1 archive ~30 GB, atlas ~3.9 GB, the v2 tape, snapshots). None of it is
# needed to replicate: every script regenerates its output from data/.
# ============================================================================

# --- Python / build / virtual-envs ---
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Secrets: ONLY .env.example is allowed ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Data: NEVER commit (the whole ~97 GB store, archive, snapshots, tapes) ---
data/
data_stage2_v1/
data_stage2_v1_*/

# --- Heavy data-file types, wherever they land in the tree ---
*.parquet
*.parquet.crc
*.jsonl
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.feather
*.arrow
*.npy
*.npz
*.h5
*.hdf5

# --- Archives / large binaries (not needed for replication) ---
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.7z

# --- Logs / runtime markers / scratch ---
*.log
data/logs/
**/.ip_penalty
_stream_parts/
_s*_tmp/

# --- Remote crawler runtime output / local env ---
deploy/remote_crawler/out/
deploy/remote_crawler/.env

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

*.bak

# Unpublished manuscript — keep OUT of git until peer-reviewed (restore/remove this line post-review)
docs/paper/

# Long-form results write-up — keep OUT of git until peer-reviewed (pre-empts the paper)
docs/research_plan_technical_report.md
docs/research_plan_technical_report.pdf

# Third-party papers / manuscripts — do NOT redistribute (cite by DOI/arXiv id instead)
docs/lieterature to review 5_11_26/
docs/16_Akey_Gregoire_Harvie_Martineau_Polymarket_author_manuscript.pdf
docs/Polymarket fee study literature taxonomy and publication roadmap.pdf
docs/Verdict *.md

# Paper-build inputs and planning artifacts (not part of the code/replication share)
*.xmind
IEEEtranBST2/
conference-latex-template/
